1. Find the process Id
      dotnet-counters ps
        12345  MyWebApi
        67890  dotnet
      Use 12345 for all commands below.

2. dotnet-counters → Quick Health Check (Live Metrics)

    Install 
    dotnet tool install --global dotnet-counters

    Monitor runtime metrices
    dotnet-counters monitor -p 12345

    This shows live:
  	•	CPU usage
	  •	GC activity
	  •	memory
	  •	threadpool
	  •	exceptions

    Example
    CPU Usage (%)
    GC Heap Size (MB)
    Gen 0 GC Count
    ThreadPool Queue Length
    Exception Count

    Monitor only runtime counters (cleaner output)
    dotnet-counters monitor -p 12345 System.Runtime

    Collect counter for specific duration
    dotnet-counters collect -p 12345 --duration 00:00:30

3. dotnet-trace → Deep CPU / Performance Analysis

   Install
    dotnet tool install --global dotnet-trace

   Collect trace
    dotnet-trace collect -p 12345

    This records:
  	•	CPU stacks
	  •	method execution
	  •	thread activity
	  •	GC events

    It produces a file:
    trace.nettrace

    Collect trace for 30 secs
    dotnet-trace collect -p 12345 --duration 00:00:30

4. dotnet-dump → Memory Leak Debugging

   Install
   dotnet tool install --global dotnet-dump

    Capture memory dump
    dotnet-dump collect -p 12345

    Creates
    core_12345.dmp
    This is a snapshot of the process memory.

    Analyze dump
    dotnet-dump analyze core_12345.dmp

    Commands for analyze
    clrstack
    dumpheap
    dumpheap -stat
    gcroot

5. Typical Production Debug Workflow

    When debugging a slow API:
    Step 1 — Check health

    dotnet-counters monitor -p <pid>

    Look for:
  	•	high CPU
	  •	high GC
	  •	threadpool queue

    Step 2 — If CPU is high
    dotnet-trace collect -p <pid> --profile cpu-sampling

    Find slow methods.

    Step 3 — If memory keeps growing
    dotnet-dump collect -p <pid>
    dotnet-dump analyze <dumpfile>

    Find leaking objects.

dotnet-counters          -> live runtime health
dotnet-trace             -> CPU & execution profiling
dotnet-dump              -> memory investigation

